<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sten Sture the Elder</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1440–1503</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sten Sture the Elder was regent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> from 1470 to 1497 and again from 1501 to 1503, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar-union">Kalmar Union</a>. His victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-i-of-denmark">Christian I of Denmark</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-brunkeberg">Battle of Brunkeberg</a> in 1471 secured his power, and he governed with the support of the peasants and miners against the pro-union nobility. In 1477 he and Archbishop Jakob Ulvsson founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppsala-university">Uppsala University</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sten-sture-the-elder.jpg" alt="Sten Sture the Elder" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Richard Mortel from Riyadh, Saudi Arabia · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stein_Gustavson_(Sture).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
